#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial is inspired by and based upon research conducted at Cleveland Clinic, as described in [Kaliakin, Danil, et al. \"Implicit solvent sample-based quantum diagonalization.\" The Journal of Physical Chemistry B 129.23 (2025): 5788-5796](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030), exposing the full workflow for implicit solvent calculations and extending it with iterative solvent self-consistency (\"The Heartwood Algorithm\", M. Motta, T. Pellegrini, 2025), geometry optimization, and automatic qubit layout selection. Please refer to the [SQD IEF-PCM Qiskit Function template](/guides/function-template-chemistry-workflow), jointly developed by Cleveland Clinic and IBM&reg; based on Cleveland Clinic research, for a streamlined, black-box interface for running implicit solvent calculations.\n"
msgstr "Este tutorial está inspirado y basado en la investigación realizada en Cleveland Clinic, como se describe en [Kaliakin, Danil, et al. \"Implicit solvent sample-based quantum diagonalization.\" The Journal of Physical Chemistry B 129.23 (2025): 5788-5796](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030), exponiendo el flujo de trabajo completo para los cálculos de solvente implícito y extendiéndolo con autoconsistencia iterativa del solvente (\"El Algoritmo Heartwood\", M. Motta, T. Pellegrini, 2025), optimización de geometría y selección automática de disposición de qubits. Por favor consulta la [plantilla de función Qiskit SQD IEF-PCM](/guides/function-template-chemistry-workflow), desarrollada conjuntamente por Cleveland Clinic e IBM&reg; basándose en la investigación de Cleveland Clinic, para obtener una interfaz simplificada de caja negra para ejecutar cálculos de solvente implícito.\n"

